Honest Conclusion:
-------------------

  The "100% match" report was WRONG.
  
  It was not a minor discrepancy or rounding error. It was a fundamental
  mischaracterization of the baseline state.
  
  The correct characterization:
    - vs b1082d7 (HEAD):       78.3% match (112/143 identical)
    - vs closest commit:        93.7% match (133/142 identical)
    - EXACT match:              does not exist in any commit
  
  The sandbox represents a DERIVED state based approximately on the v5.1.0
  merge, with additional schema, code, and test modifications applied
  independently.
  
  This finding means:
    a) All prior work built on the "100% match" assumption is suspect
    b) Migration chain divergence is explained (sandbox lacks 0015/0016)
    c) The 31 file differences are real, not artifacts
    d) Recovery planning must account for BOTH trees, not assume identity

